ggml-cpu simd-gemm: use the 4x4 register tile on arm64 (__ARM_NEON, not __ARM_NEON__)

simd-gemm.h tests __ARM_NEON__, which only 32-bit ARM compilers define. aarch64 clang (NDK r29) defines
__ARM_NEON, so arm64 builds fell back to GEMM_RM = GEMM_RN = 2. The tiled flash-attention kernel that runs every
prefill then had 4 FMA chains instead of 16. The 4x4 tile adds the same terms in the same order, so results should
stay bit-identical. arm64 under QEMU (MiniCPM5 and Ling, with 0001-0004): KL divergence against stock at the
tool's floor (max 3.7e-5, same top token 100%).

Expected: flash attention is about half of each prefill token's time at depth 1,100 on a Pixel 10 (derived, MiniCPM5
and Ling); phone measurement pending. Upstream master still has the bug; no PR yet.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-gemm.h b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-gemm.h
index 4b9396d54..9076cc3d8 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-gemm.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-gemm.h
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 
 // TODO: untested on avx512
 // These are in units of GGML_F32_EPR
-#if defined(__AVX512F__) || defined (__ARM_NEON__)
+#if defined(__AVX512F__) || defined(__ARM_NEON)
     static constexpr int GEMM_RM = 4;
     static constexpr int GEMM_RN = 4; // 16+4+1 = 25/32
 #elif defined(__AVX2__) || defined(__AVX__)
